# Ozma RPA script: Bootstrap Windows Rust node (ozma-node --profile desktop)
#
# Everything comes from the USB drive (E:\) delivered by the soft node / QEMU.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - bash dev/windows-vm/prepare-media.sh  (stages Rust workspace + vendored crates)
#   - bash dev/windows-vm/provision.sh create  (starts Windows VM)
#   - Windows booted and at desktop (autounattend.xml handles this)
#
# What's on the USB drive (E:\):
#   rust/           rustup-init.exe
#   ozma/src/       Rust workspace (ozma-node + workspace crates + vendor/)
#   ozma/           install-offline.ps1, install-offline.bat, controller.txt
#   viostor/        Virtio drivers (used during Windows install)

log === Ozma Windows Rust Node Self-Bootstrap ===

# Wait for Windows desktop
log Waiting for Windows desktop...
wait_for_text taskbar
sleep 10

# Open PowerShell as administrator
log Opening PowerShell as admin...
key win+x
sleep 1
key a
sleep 3
# Accept UAC if it appears
key left
key enter
sleep 3

# Wait for PowerShell prompt
wait_for_text PS C:\
sleep 1

# Run the offline Rust bootstrap script from the USB drive
log Running Rust self-bootstrap script from USB drive...
type Set-ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Scope Process -Force\n
sleep 2
type for ($d in 'D','E','F','G') { if (Test-Path "${d}:\ozma\install-offline.ps1") { & "${d}:\ozma\install-offline.ps1"; break } }\n

# Wait for Rust toolchain check/install + cargo test + cargo build --release
log Waiting for Rust toolchain & cargo test/build...
sleep 120

# Wait for completion marker
wait_for_text === Complete ===
sleep 5

# Verify the built .exe was staged back to the USB drive
type dir E:\ozma\ozma-node.exe\n
sleep 3

log === Windows Rust node self-bootstrap complete ===
log Built .exe is at C:\Program Files\Ozma\Node\ozma-node.exe and E:\ozma\ozma-node.exe
